# BELLA HEALTHCARE & EDUCATION OS — CURSOR RULES & AI FIREWALL

# READ CONSTITUTIONS BEFORE ANY HEALTHCARE OR EDUCATION CODING:
# Healthcare Path: docs/architecture/HEALTHCARE_VERTICAL_CODING_CONSTITUTION.md
# Education Path: docs/architecture/EDUCATION_VERTICAL_CODING_CONSTITUTION.md

## 1. SHARED CORE LAWS
- Common Core (`src/platform/core/` and generic platform engines) must remain domain-agnostic. No references to Patient, Encounter, Course, Student, GPA, etc.

## 2. HEALTHCARE OS LAWS
- KERNEL H1-H12 IS FROZEN. NEVER CREATE H13 OR NEW KERNEL ENGINES.
- PRODUCT LOGIC LIVES ONLY IN src/products/ OR src/platform/healthcare/verticals/.
- PRODUCT CONSUMES KERNEL ONLY VIA PUBLIC CONTRACTS. NO DIRECT QUERY ON hc_* KERNEL TABLES.
- MIGRATIONS MUST BE ADDITIVE ONLY. NO ALTER/DROP ON KERNEL TABLES.
- NO DUPLICATE KERNEL ENTITIES (Patient, Doctor, Encounter).
- NO 'any' TYPES ALLOWED.
- RUN 'npm run healthcare:verify' BEFORE SUBMITTING.

## 3. EDUCATION OS LAWS
- EDUCATION OS KERNEL IS FROZEN. NO CODES/MIGRATIONS CAN BE MUTATED WITHOUT ARCHITECTURE APPROVAL.
- PRODUCT LOGIC LIVES ONLY IN src/products/ OR src/platform/education/.
- EDUCATION PRODUCT CONSUMES EDUCATION KERNEL ONLY VIA CONTRACTS.
- NO DUPLICATE KERNEL ENTITIES (Course, Enrollment, Student Role).
- NO 'any' TYPES ALLOWED.

## 4. NO CROSS-INDUSTRY COUPLING
- Education OS is strictly prohibited from importing or depending on Healthcare OS code or tables.
- Healthcare OS is strictly prohibited from importing or depending on Education OS code or tables.
- Cross-industry dependencies are blocked. Both systems must interact only with Shared Platform Core and platform public contracts.
